.TH JOBWRAP 1 "August 2026" "jobwrap 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jobwrap \- wrap a locally launched Linux process with monitoring and control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jobwrap
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR...]
.br
.B jobwrap \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBjobwrap\fR runs \fICOMMAND\fR inside a pseudo-terminal so it behaves exactly
like a normal foreground command, while a per-user daemon provides a web
interface, an HTTP API, and scoped control of the process.
.PP
If the first word is not a recognized subcommand it is treated as the command
to run, so \fBjobwrap python3 analysis.py\fR works directly. Use
\fBjobwrap -- COMMAND\fR to make that explicit.
.SH WRAPPER OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-name \fINAME\fR
A human-readable name for the job.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fINAME\fR
The access profile to use (defaults to the configured profile).
.TP
.B \-\-detach
Detach from the terminal and run in the background.
.TP
.B \-\-no-web
Do not start or use the web server.
.TP
.B \-\-no-record
Do not record terminal output to the log.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List registered jobs.
.TP
.B show \fIJOB\fR
Show detailed information about one job.
.TP
.B logs \fIJOB\fR [\-\-offset N]
Print a job's recorded output.
.TP
.B signal \fIJOB\fR \fISIGNAL\fR
Send a named signal (int, term, stop, cont, kill) to a job's process group.
.TP
.B stop \fIJOB\fR
Send SIGTERM to a job's process group.
.TP
.B open [\fIJOB\fR]
Open the web interface in a browser.
.TP
.B daemon status|start|stop
Manage the per-user daemon.
.TP
.B config init|validate|effective|explain
Manage the configuration.
.TP
.B auth set-password|remove-password|status
Manage the browser password.
.TP
.B token create|list|revoke
Manage scoped API tokens.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The wrapper returns the child's exit code. Signals are reported as 128 plus the
signal number. Internal failures before the child starts use dedicated codes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/jobwrap/config.toml
Configuration (see \fBjobwrap.toml(5)\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/jobwrap/daemon.sock
The private daemon socket.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/jobwrap/jobwrap.db
SQLite database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/jobwrap/logs/
Append-only terminal logs.
.SH SECURITY
See \fI/usr/share/doc/jobwrap/README.md\fR and the security model. The daemon
binds to loopback by default and never creates arbitrary processes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jobwrapd (8),
.BR jobwrap.toml (5)
